    fix(int-ci-030): hermetic git config for push-gate tests; kill9 walk skips .search index
    
    - PUSH-001 (autocommit-push-gate.test.ts): the host GLOBAL git config
      (core.hooksPath=<agent hooks dir>) is also read by git receive-pack on
      file:// pushes, overriding the bare remote own hooks/post-receive push
      counter - pushCount() read 0 on this host while CI stayed green. Point
      GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL/GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM at empty scratch files for the test
      process so both ends of the push are hermetic.
    - durability-kill9.test.ts: jsonlFiles() counted the rebuildable .search/
      index stub (rows.tmp.jsonl, created at daemon boot by aug-096 commit
      32de0244) as a second partition file - the length 1 got 2 duplicates and
      the empty files[0] in the graceful case. Skip .search alongside
      .git/_audit. Durability guarantee untouched; root cause documented in a
      test comment per INT-CI-030 AC-2.
    
    Guard attribution (TS-only diff vs Python-scoped gitreins guard, per
    ts-only-commit-vs-python-scoped-guard): diff mode maps engine/foo.py to
    tests/test_foo.py only, so this two-.ts staged set is unmatchable; the
    commit-time run was secrets=clean + tests SKIP (DEGRADED PASS, hook exit 1).
    Gates run manually in lieu of the skipped lane:
    - pnpm vitest run src/git/autocommit-push-gate.test.ts: 12 passed, 3
      consecutive runs on this host (AC-1)
    - pnpm vitest run src/storage/durability-kill9.test.ts: 3 passed
    - pnpm vitest run src/http/routes/memories-dogfood010.test.ts: 3 passed x5
      runs (one-off CI timeout documented, no change)
    - pnpm tsc --noEmit: clean (AC-4)
    - pnpm test:run (full): 1841 passed, 3 failed - all 3 pre-existing baseline
      reds (namespace-warmup-aug096 + ddl-views), reproduced at clean HEAD (AC-5)
    
    Verified: push-gate 3x green; kill9 green locally; dogfood010 5x green.
